AquaStream360 Network Transformation Module Guide

What This Module Does
The Network Transformation Module allows you to visually manipulate your water distribution network’s spatial layout. You can translate (move), rotate, scale, flip, and reflect your entire network while seeing real-time previews in both traditional plotting views and interactive GIS maps.
Key Concepts to Understand
1. Coordinate System
•	Original Coordinates: Your network’s current geographical positions
•	Transformed Coordinates: Modified positions after applying transformations
•	World Units: Coordinates are typically in meters or feet (preserved from your .inp file)
2. Transformation Types
•	Translation: Moving the network along X and Y axes
•	Rotation: Spinning the network around a central point
•	Scaling: Enlarging or shrinking the entire network
•	Reflection: Mirroring the network across X or Y axes
3. Visualization Modes
•	GIS Map: Interactive map with satellite/street views
•	Both: Split-screen view for comparison
