Important Considerations
What Gets Transformed
•	Node coordinates (X,Y positions)
•	Visual representation of pipes/valves
•	Pipe lengths (remain unchanged)
•	Elevation data (Z coordinates if present)
•	Network connectivity or attributes
Transformation Order
The system applies transformations in this sequence: 1. Scaling (enlargement/shrinking) 2. Reflection (flipping) 3. Rotation (around center point) 4. Translation (final positioning)
This order ensures predictable results.
Undo/Redo Capability
•	Reset: Reverts all transformations to original state
•	Before Apply: Unlimited experimentation
•	After Apply: Changes are permanent to the network
•	Recommendation: Test thoroughly before applying
